Science Against Authoritarianism (Pharos) — License Index
=========================================================

Copyright (c) 2026 The Pharos contributors

Pharos is a project for the public, built for the good of humanity and
the environment. It is offered free of charge, and its contributors
seek no personal recognition; the attribution the licenses require
goes to "The Pharos contributors".


This repository is multi-licensed. Different file types are governed
by different SPDX-identified licenses, chosen to match the norms of
each content type:

  • Reports, manuscripts, prose, research deliverables (.md, .tex,
    .pdf, plain prose) — Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0
    International (CC BY-SA 4.0). Copyleft: derivatives must also be
    CC BY-SA 4.0.
    Canonical text: LICENSES/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt

  • Code (.py, .sh, .ipynb, Makefile, CI workflows) — GNU General
    Public License version 3.0 or later (GPL-3.0-or-later). Copyleft:
    derivatives that link or integrate this code must release source
    under GPL-3.0-or-later.
    Canonical text: LICENSES/GPL-3.0-or-later.txt

  • Numerical outputs and fact tables (.csv, .json, derived metrics
    from open datasets) — Creative Commons Zero 1.0 Universal
    (CC0 1.0). Public-domain dedication.
    Canonical text: LICENSES/CC0-1.0.txt

  • Web files (.html, .css, .js) — licensed per file by their inline
    SPDX headers: the observatory app code (site/app/app.js,
    site/app/style.css) is GPL-3.0-or-later; the page markup and the
    landing page (site/app/index.html, site/index.html, site/style.css)
    are CC BY-SA 4.0.

Every file's license is given by its inline SPDX header or, where it
has none, by REUSE.toml. The project follows the REUSE specification
(https://reuse.software).

For the project's statement of original contributions, attribution,
AI/ML training notice, and ethical-use covenant, see NOTICE.


A note on third-party data
--------------------------

This project analyses open, third-party data: the World Bank Worldwide
Governance Indicators, and V-Dem and Freedom House series via Our World
in Data. Those datasets carry their own licenses and citation
requirements and are NOT relicensed by this repository. Small pinned
extracts are redistributed in data/snapshots/ under their upstream
licenses, only so the pipeline reproduces offline (see REUSE.toml);
credit each dataset to its own source under its own terms. The
project's original analysis, code, prose, and derived figures are
covered by the licenses above.


